  "connections": "The series features recurring segments like Deep Dive, Examples, Challenges, Predictions, and Listener Questions across the episodes [Deep Dive, Examples, Challenges, Predictions, Listener Question]. Mark Rivera referenced external examples like GitLab, Automattic, and Doist which provide written handbooks supporting async culture [L02]. Hannah Okafor built directly on Rivera's concepts by focusing on practical application, detailing how to build a writing culture and addressing documentation rot [L13]. The conversation consistently linked documentation to tangible results, such as reducing meeting time and accelerating new hire ramp-up [L11, L12]. Both episodes emphasized moving away from tool reliance towards a culture driven by written norms. Tom Becker’s input in ep005 contrasted the engineering focus on outcomes with the realities faced by support roles, contrasting outcome measurement with coverage necessity [L19, L20]. Recurring guests include Mark Rivera and Hannah Okafor, who developed the framework from high-level philosophy to actionable writing habits. The discussion across episodes links documentation to operational success, whether in async communication or managing team presence.",
